entalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The book frames violence against women as an epidemic connected to gender roles and presents recovery from abuse as a difficult, ongoing struggle.","confidence":0.78},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.9},"profileConfidence":0.95,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"c67a47ce554305312c42470696cf04d1fea05247b1c8e92deae7510d97643187","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-the-other-side-lacy-m-johnson.jpg","primarySubject":"Biography","secondarySubjects":["Gender & Sexuality","True Crime & Justice"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book is a first-person account of Lacy M. Johnson's harrowing experience as a kidnapping victim, fitting firmly within Memoir & Autobiography while also addressing issues of gender violence and true crime.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"3ea0d249552a3b87b1a6d3ca1d70a3b2a3841defbdf05074da49c2c603d85b18","summary":"\"Lacy Johnson was held prisoner in a soundproofed room in a basement apartment that her ex-boyfriend rented and outfitted for the sole purpose of raping and killing her. She escaped, but not unscathed. The Other Side is the haunting account of a first passionate and then abusive relationship, the events leading to Johnson's kidnapping and imprisonment, her dramatic escape, and her hard-fought struggle to recover. At once thrilling, terrifying, harrowing, and hopeful, The Other Side offers more than just a true crime record. In language both stark and poetic, Johnson weaves together a richly personal narrative with police reports, psychological evaluations, and neurobiological investigations, provoking both troubling and timely questions about gender roles and the epidemic of violence against women. \"--","pageCount":219,"publicationYear":2014,"displaySummary":"The Other Side is the haunting account of a f